2025-05-01 03:30:24 - Thread-1450 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• deliveries.delivery_id : unique delivery record – each row represents one delivery to be counted  
• deliveries.driver_id : identifies which driver performed the delivery (key field for the ranking)  
• deliveries.delivery_status : lets us keep only completed rows (e.g. 'DELIVERED')  
• deliveries.delivery_order_id : foreign‑key that links a delivery row to its order row  
• orders.order_id : primary key that matches deliveries.delivery_order_id  
• orders.order_created_day / _month / _year : give us the calendar day on which the delivery occurred; grouping by those three columns lets us build a “daily” grain without any date‑time parsing  
• orders.order_status / orders.order_moment_delivered : extra filters to keep only finished orders  
• drivers.driver_modal / drivers.driver_type : descriptive fields, useful for later enrichment or additional filters  

Typical conditions you will probably apply later  

• deliveries.delivery_status = 'DELIVERED'                 – insure the job was completed  
• orders.order_status      = 'DELIVERED'                   – optional extra safeguard  
• orders.order_created_year = 2021 …                       – pick a time window if needed  

------------------------------------------------------------
Exploratory queries (all limited to 20 rows)  
Each query is standalone and slightly more sophisticated than the previous one.

```sql
--Description: 1) Inspect a handful of delivery rows and see the basic columns we will use
SELECT *
FROM "deliveries"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Look at the distinct delivery statuses that exist
SELECT DISTINCT "delivery_status"
FROM "deliveries"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) List the available drivers and their attributes
SELECT DISTINCT d."driver_id",
                d."driver_modal",
                d."driver_type"
FROM "drivers" AS d
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Quick count of total deliveries completed by each driver (no date grain yet)
SELECT d."driver_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "total_deliveries"
FROM "deliveries" AS d
WHERE d."delivery_status" = 'DELIVERED'
GROUP BY d."driver_id"
ORDER BY "total_deliveries" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Check how delivery rows join to orders, confirming the relationship
SELECT dl."delivery_id",
       dl."driver_id",
       o."order_id",
       o."order_status"
FROM   "deliveries" AS dl
JOIN   "orders"     AS o
       ON o."order_id" = dl."delivery_order_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Count deliveries per driver per calendar day
SELECT dl."driver_id",
       o."order_created_year",
       o."order_created_month",
       o."order_created_day",
       COUNT(*) AS "deliveries_that_day"
FROM   "deliveries" AS dl
JOIN   "orders"     AS o
       ON o."order_id" = dl."delivery_order_id"
WHERE  dl."delivery_status" = 'DELIVERED'
GROUP  BY dl."driver_id",
          o."order_created_year",
          o."order_created_month",
          o."order_created_day"
ORDER  BY "deliveries_that_day" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Average daily deliveries for each driver
SELECT daily."driver_id",
       AVG(daily."deliveries_that_day") AS "avg_daily_deliveries"
FROM (
        SELECT dl."driver_id",
               o."order_created_year",
               o."order_created_month",
               o."order_created_day",
               COUNT(*) AS "deliveries_that_day"
        FROM   "deliveries" AS dl
        JOIN   "orders"     AS o
               ON o."order_id" = dl."delivery_order_id"
        WHERE  dl."delivery_status" = 'DELIVERED'
        GROUP  BY dl."driver_id",
                  o."order_created_year",
                  o."order_created_month",
                  o."order_created_day"
     ) AS daily
GROUP BY daily."driver_id"
ORDER BY "avg_daily_deliveries" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Same as #7 but bringing driver type for context
SELECT a."driver_id",
       dr."driver_type",
       dr."driver_modal",
       a."avg_daily_deliveries"
FROM (
        SELECT daily."driver_id",
               AVG(daily."deliveries_that_day") AS "avg_daily_deliveries"
        FROM (
                SELECT dl."driver_id",
                       o."order_created_year",
                       o."order_created_month",
                       o."order_created_day",
                       COUNT(*) AS "deliveries_that_day"
                FROM   "deliveries" AS dl
                JOIN   "orders"     AS o
                       ON o."order_id" = dl."delivery_order_id"
                WHERE  dl."delivery_status" = 'DELIVERED'
                GROUP  BY dl."driver_id",
                          o."order_created_year",
                          o."order_created_month",
                          o."order_created_day"
             ) AS daily
        GROUP BY daily."driver_id"
     ) AS a
LEFT JOIN "drivers" AS dr
       ON dr."driver_id" = a."driver_id"
ORDER BY a."avg_daily_deliveries" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Top‑5 drivers with the highest average number of daily deliveries
SELECT a."driver_id",
       a."avg_daily_deliveries"
FROM (
        SELECT daily."driver_id",
               AVG(daily."deliveries_that_day") AS "avg_daily_deliveries"
        FROM (
                SELECT dl."driver_id",
                       o."order_created_year",
                       o."order_created_month",
                       o."order_created_day",
                       COUNT(*) AS "deliveries_that_day"
                FROM   "deliveries" AS dl
                JOIN   "orders"     AS o
                       ON o."order_id" = dl."delivery_order_id"
                WHERE  dl."delivery_status" = 'DELIVERED'
                GROUP  BY dl."driver_id",
                          o."order_created_year",
                          o."order_created_month",
                          o."order_created_day"
             ) AS daily
        GROUP BY daily."driver_id"
     ) AS a
ORDER BY a."avg_daily_deliveries" DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Same top‑5 list, enriched with driver attributes
SELECT a."driver_id",
       dr."driver_modal",
       dr."driver_type",
       a."avg_daily_deliveries"
FROM (
        SELECT daily."driver_id",
               AVG(daily."deliveries_that_day") AS "avg_daily_deliveries"
        FROM (
                SELECT dl."driver_id",
                       o."order_created_year",
                       o."order_created_month",
                       o."order_created_day",
                       COUNT(*) AS "deliveries_that_day"
                FROM   "deliveries" AS dl
                JOIN   "orders"     AS o
                       ON o."order_id" = dl."delivery_order_id"
                WHERE  dl."delivery_status" = 'DELIVERED'
                GROUP  BY dl."driver_id",
                          o."order_created_year",
                          o."order_created_month",
                          o."order_created_day"
             ) AS daily
        GROUP BY daily."driver_id"
     ) AS a
LEFT JOIN "drivers" AS dr
       ON dr."driver_id" = a."driver_id"
ORDER BY a."avg_daily_deliveries" DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

